Chapter: CapHeapPokePure

 Positive guard for the capability granularity ruling (CapabilityProbe
 section 7.3): peek-byte and poke-byte access the program's OWN heap,
 and heap access is not I/O - they stay pure by design, even in
 enforced application code. This is deliberate, not a laundering hole:
 the type system cannot distinguish a heap address from a device
 register at a runtime value, so memory-mapped device I/O gets its own
 read-mmio / poke-mmio intrinsics carrying Device.Mmio (the error case
 lives in errors/cap-launder-pure-mmio). A pure-signature function
 using the heap intrinsics must keep compiling.

Section: Definitions

  raw-mem : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  raw-mem (addr) (val) =
   let w = poke-byte addr 0 val
   in peek-byte addr 0

  opening : Text = show (raw-mem 786432 42)

